<title>USA: Staples, Office Depot delay meetings.</title>
<headline>Staples, Office Depot delay meetings.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBOROUGH, Mass. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Staples Inc said on Thursday that it and Office Depot Inc agreed with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission to extend the Hart Scott Rodino waiting period on their proposed merger on a one-week rolling basis.</p>
<p>The extension is intended to give the FTC ample time to consider the companies' proposed sale of 63 stores to OfficeMax Inc, which is meant to allay FTC concerns about the merger.</p>
<p>The two companies also said they intend to adjourn their special shareholder meetings scheduled for Friday, until March 31.</p>
</text>
